{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And the house shall be … permanent.</b> It has gone out of the power of the seller and stands in the power of the buyer." "<b>That has no wall.</b> We read it לוֹ — 'his.' Our Rabbis of blessed memory said: even though he does not have it now, since he did have it previously. And עִיר is feminine, so it should have required לָהּ — 'hers.' But since לֹא — 'not' — had to be written in the text, they fixed לוֹ in the masoretic reading — the one falls upon the other." "<b>It shall not go out in the Jubilee.</b> Rav Safra said: If the Jubilee befell it within its [two-]year [redemption] window, it does not go out (see Arakhin 31)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {1 "Rashi explains the ketiv (לא) and qere (לו): the written form לא is read as לו; and since עיר is feminine, one would expect לה — but the consonants ל-ו/ל-א overlap, so the masoretic reading לו was set in place of לה."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:25.035503327Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}